&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What Enterprise Email Marketing Software Must Do&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Enterprise &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/benefits-of-email-marketing"&gt;email marketing&lt;/a&gt; software must support complex, multi-team programs without weakening control. The platform should make campaigns easier to scale while keeping customer data, consent, brand standards, and reporting intact. These six capabilities separate enterprise-ready platforms from email tools with generous contact limits.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;Enforce governance and security controls.&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Consent records must show when, where, and how each contact subscribed. Consent records that show when, where, and how each contact subscribed protect the company when data moves across brands, regions, or integrations. Enterprise marketing teams cannot afford to underestimate security controls. For example, in the UK, two companies were fined &lt;a href="https://ico.org.uk/about-the-ico/media-centre/news-and-blogs/2024/10/two-companies-fined-a-total-of-150k-after-bombarding-people-with-spam-texts-offering-financial-debt-services/"&gt;£150,000&lt;/a&gt; for sending 7.5 million unwanted messages. Third-party suppliers were unable to prove valid consent.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Enterprise email marketing teams have to ensure their software has these features:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Role-based permissions&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;SSO and two-factor authentication&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Campaign approvals&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Audit logs&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Asset partitioning&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Sandbox environments&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Global businesses should also check regional data hosting, encryption, data retention, and support for deletion requests.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;Connect email activity to CRM revenue data.&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Email metrics lose value when campaign data sits apart from the CRM, making it hard to trace results to revenue. CRM-native email marketing platforms prevent this by keeping engagement, lifecycle stage, company data, deals, and revenue on connected records, enabling clear revenue attribution.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/marketing"&gt;Marketing Hub&lt;/a&gt;, operating on &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/crm/ai-crm"&gt;HubSpot&amp;nbsp;Smart CRM&lt;/a&gt; data, lets marketers create attribution reports and connect email marketing interactions to deal creation and won revenue, giving marketing and sales one dataset to work from.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;Support ABM and multi-brand operations.&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/customers/how-to-use-marketing-email-in-your-account-based-marketing-strategy"&gt;Account-based marketing&lt;/a&gt; (ABM) targets companies, but email reaches individual people. Enterprise email software must connect those two levels. It should group consented contacts under an account, recognize their roles, and adjust nurture emails as the deal progresses.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Enterprise email software enables this coordination. For example, it can alert sales when several stakeholders engage, switch content after an opportunity opens, or pause marketing emails during active sales conversations.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The same coordination matters across multi-brand companies. Each brand may need its own domains, consent preferences, templates, and sender reputation, while leadership still needs shared customer data and reporting. HubSpot’s &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/marketing/multi-account-management"&gt;multi-account management&lt;/a&gt;, available at the Enterprise level, solves this by keeping business accounts separate while allowing data, assets, workflows, and reports to move across them based on configured connections.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/best-email-marketing-software-for-enterprises-2-20261002-7091357.webp?width=650&amp;amp;height=291&amp;amp;name=best-email-marketing-software-for-enterprises-2-20261002-7091357.webp" width="650" height="291" alt="HubSpot enterprise email marketing software multi-account management screen for sharing approved data, assets, reports, and workflows across two business accounts." style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;Apply AI to high-friction workflows.&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Personalized email at enterprise scale requires more than a good subject line. &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/ai-email-marketing"&gt;AI in enterprise email marketing&lt;/a&gt; handles the infrastructure behind it: audience creation, CRM data classification, workflow design, campaign QA, and send-time optimization.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;HubSpot’s AI tools can help marketers &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/marketing/audience-segments"&gt;build segment filters&lt;/a&gt;, then map and &lt;a href="https://knowledge.hubspot.com/workflows/use-ai-to-manage-data-in-workflows"&gt;create workflows&lt;/a&gt;, summarize CRM data, and update or categorize records. Th...

&lt;p&gt;Today, when a buyer asks ChatGPT, Perplexity, or Google’s AI Mode a question, they rarely see a list of suggested links. They see one synthesized answer that cites a handful of sources. If your brand is one of those citations, you win attention, traffic, and trust. If it isn’t, you’re invisible, even when you rank on page one.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=07ca2318-c9e0-4b5d-bcba-95cec5cb4958&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Download Now: The State of AEO in 2026 [Free AI Search Trends Report]" height="79" width="369" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/07ca2318-c9e0-4b5d-bcba-95cec5cb4958.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;That shift matters for revenue teams who need to reach those buyers. Referral traffic from AI tools like ChatGPT and Gemini has tripled over the past year, and &lt;a href="https://offers.hubspot.com/state-of-aeo"&gt;44% of marketers&lt;/a&gt; say they’ve made a business purchase based on a brand they first discovered in an AI answer. Nearly 1/3 have done it more than once. The audience didn’t disappear; it moved into the answer.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;In this guide, we explain how AI search optimization actually works: How AI answer engines retrieve, ground, cite, and evaluate content, and what brands need to do to make their content easier for AI systems to retrieve, understand, and cite. Also included: A side-by-side comparison of AI search optimization versus classic SEO, quick wins you can implement this week, and expert tips from practitioners on the Found in AI podcast.&lt;/p&gt; 
